ope for the direct digest/OAuth2 calls) fails the test while vault.GetCredentialResponse lacks EgressScope, so the file compiles and runs at the base with every test red by assertion - no panic, no missing symbol. The previous attempt's rejection is fixed: TestPublicScopeIgnoresProxyEnvironmentChild now fails at the base too (field check before the marker guard), and passes only in green. TestScopeArrivesFromVault drives the generic and classical-key flows through startScopedFakeVault with one header pair per scope (public -> 502 not-allowed; any / no header -> reach the server; two any pairs -> 502 again), so the header-reading path is exercised without touching internal/vault. TestPublicScopeRefusesNonPublicTargets runs all 23 scenario targets through all five flows and asserts the local server's count stays 0; each flow call carries a five-second request context, which also covers the .invalid and child scenarios' named tolerance. Scoped credential values reuse the built-from-parts vars of stored_target_test.go; no secret-shaped literal is written. The public side of IsPublicIP, several-address resolution and the checked-IP property have no test, as design 'Risks' says none is promised.", "criteria": {"C-0770d694": {"tests": ["github.com/mintkey/mintkey/services/proxy-plugin/cmd/proxy-plugin::TestPublicScopeIgnoresProxyEnvironment_C_0770d694"], "proof": "red_assertion", "discriminating": ["github.com/mintkey/mintkey/services/proxy-plugin/cmd/proxy-plugin::TestPublicScopeIgnoresProxyEnvironment_C_0770d694"]}, "C-37681a78": {"tests": ["github.com/mintkey/mintkey/services/proxy-plugin/cmd/proxy-plugin::TestPublicScopeRefusesLoopbackName_C_37681a78"], "proof": "red_assertion", "discriminating": ["github.com/mintkey/mintkey/services/proxy-plugin/cmd/proxy-plugin::TestPublicScopeRefusesLoopbackName_C_37681a78"]}, "C-b5f6f1f1": {"tests": ["github.com/mintkey/mintkey/services/proxy-plugin/cmd/proxy-plugin::TestScopeArrivesFromVault_C_b5f6f1f1"], "proof": "red_assertion",